From e4cafb74b49180e0613a996c7bdfec74959ee24f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:35:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Treasure Trails: hard clue scrolls and the hard casket

TrailTier.Hard on the same engine: 4-6 steps from the cache's hard cluehelper rows, one scroll
obj per step; anagram and cipher talks with challenge scrolls, cryptic talks/searches/digs,
coordinate digs, the 7 hard maps (map05/08/12/13/14 and trail_clue_hard_map006/007, matched by
rendering the interfaces against the OSRS Wiki's map images), single emotes with the hard Uri,
music steps, hard STASH units (Construction 55, teak planks, 400 XP). The hard casket (dbtable
trail_hard_casket, 234 rows) is the wiki table flattened over 6,971,393 with 4-6 rolls.
Not yet: puzzle boxes (those 5 anagram rows are left out, as is the one anagram whose target is
a loc), the coordinate wizards and the Double agent (coordinates dig straight away, Uri comes at
once), the master clue tertiary. Integration tests.
